.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OPENSSL-GENDSA 1ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openssl-gendsa
.Nd generate a DSA private key from a set of parameters
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm openssl
.Ar gendsa
.Oo
.Fl help ]
.Oo
.Fl out
.Em filename ]
.Oo
.Fl passout
.Em arg ]
.Oo
.Fl aes128 ]
.Oo
.Fl aes192 ]
.Oo
.Fl aes256 ]
.Oo
.Fl aria128 ]
.Oo
.Fl aria192 ]
.Oo
.Fl aria256 ]
.Oo
.Fl camellia128 ]
.Oo
.Fl camellia192 ]
.Oo
.Fl camellia256 ]
.Oo
.Fl des ]
.Oo
.Fl des3 ]
.Oo
.Fl idea ]
.Oo
.Fl verbose ]
.Oo
.Fl quiet ]
.Oo
.Fl rand
.Em files ]
.Oo
.Fl writerand
.Em file ]
.Oo
.Fl engine
.Em id ]
.Oo
.Fl provider
.Em name ]
.Oo
.Fl provider-path
.Em path ]
.Oo
.Fl provparam
.Em [name:]key=value ]
.Oo
.Fl propquery
.Em propq ]
.Oo
.Em paramfile ]
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command generates a DSA private key from a DSA parameter file
(which will be typically generated by the
.Xr openssl-dsaparam 1
command).
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help
Print out a usage message.
.It Sy -out Em filename
Output the key to the specified file.
If this argument is not specified then standard output is used.
.It Sy -passout Em arg
The passphrase used for the output file.
See
.Xr openssl-passphrase-options 1 .
.It Sy -aes128 Ns , Sy -aes192 Ns , Sy -aes256 Ns , Sy -aria128 Ns , Sy -aria192 Ns , Sy -aria256 Ns , Sy -camellia128 Ns , Sy -camellia192 Ns , Sy -camellia256 Ns , Sy -des Ns , Sy -des3 Ns , Sy -idea
These options encrypt the private key with specified cipher before
outputting it.
A pass phrase is prompted for.
If none of these options is specified no encryption is used.
.Pp
Note that all options must be given before the
.Em paramfile
argument.
.It Sy -verbose
Print extra details about the operations being performed.
.It Sy -quiet
Print fewer details about the operations being performed, which may be
handy during batch scripts and pipelines.
.It Sy -rand Em files Ns , Sy -writerand Em file
See
.Xr openssl 1
for details.
.It Sy -engine Em id
See
.Xr openssl 1 .
This option is deprecated.
.It Em paramfile
The DSA parameter file to use.
The parameters in this file determine the size of the private key.
DSA parameters can be generated and examined using the
.Xr openssl-dsaparam 1
command.
.It Sy -provider Em name
.It Sy -provider-path Em path
.It Sy -provparam Em [name:]key=value
.It Sy -propquery Em propq
See
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
and
.Xr property 7 .
.El
.Sh NOTES
DSA key generation is little more than random number generation so it is
much quicker that RSA key generation for example.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr openssl-genpkey 1 ,
.Xr openssl-dsaparam 1 ,
.Xr openssl-dsa 1 ,
.Xr openssl-genrsa 1 ,
.Xr openssl-rsa 1
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Sy -engine
option was deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
